Authoritative operator acceptance and restrictions (native comment 351):
Hermes: preserve this card as a staged implementation/qualification task. Do NOT launch the live residency smoke yet.

The card has two distinct acceptance layers:

STAGE A — offline harness implementation and review

STAGE B — explicitly approved live A/B residency smoke

Passing Stage A does NOT complete the card, because the original contract explicitly requires real measured A/B smoke evidence.

Likewise, failure to run Stage B yet does NOT justify repeating Stage A from scratch.

## Stage A — finish and independently verify offline deliverables

First inspect the retained workspace and recover existing implementation before writing anything new.

The Stage A deliverable should be durable and self-contained, including at minimum:

- harness source;
- configuration/preset rendering for A and B;
- metrics/result schema;
- mocked model lifecycle;
- mocked residency/load/eviction observations;
- OOM/error classification;
- raw-log capture logic;
- protocol/version identity;
- fixture data;
- offline tests;
- reproducible README/exact commands.

The offline suite should prove, without model execution:

1. Condition A represents monster-alone.
2. Condition B represents monster + utility configuration.
3. The harness does not equate “configured” with “resident”.
4. Actual residency requires runtime evidence.
5. A missing/evicted utility model is visible in results.
6. A monster eviction/reload is visible rather than silently accepted.
7. OOM/Metal errors abort appropriately.
8. Metrics are written in the documented machine-readable schema.
9. Invalid/incomplete runs cannot accidentally produce PASS.
10. A/B configurations preserve all controls except the intended residency difference.
11. Production router `:18434` is never targeted by default.
12. `models_max`, wired-memory limit and production profiles/config are never modified by Stage A.

Run the complete offline test suite and preserve raw output.

Then request independent review of Stage A.

Do not mark the whole card DONE after Stage A.

A truthful intermediate state is:

`offline_harness_complete = true`
`offline_harness_reviewed = true`
`live_smoke_complete = false`
`goal_terminal = false`

## Revalidate the parent protocol before Stage B

The parent residency protocol was written against a specific monster/goblin choice and configuration.

Before live execution, confirm that its assumptions still match current operator intent and reviewed evidence.

Do not silently substitute models because current routing/config has changed.

Specifically verify:

- exact monster model/file/quantisation;
- exact utility model/file/quantisation;
- context sizes;
- llama.cpp/runtime build;
- memory/residency measurement method;
- trial count and warm-up;
- pass/fail thresholds;
- workload/task definitions.

If the operator has subsequently chosen different candidate models, update the protocol deliberately before running rather than treating a stale preset as authority.

## Stage B remains explicitly approval-gated

Do NOT perform any live model-load smoke until Adrian explicitly approves an exclusive local execution window.

Current overnight cloud policy is not permission to run this local experiment.

The residency trial consumes unified memory and may destabilise the same host used by valuable local work.

Before approval, require:

- host-wide local-worker budget reviewed/enforced;
- no valuable local model session active;
- safe recovery owner identified;
- router/runtime recovery procedure prepared;
- exact abort thresholds pre-registered;
- no other model-loading experiment sharing the window.

## Live topology

Do not bypass `models_max=1` by casually starting a hidden side server while another valuable model is resident.

The parent protocol’s isolated benchmark router is acceptable only during the explicitly authorised exclusive experiment window and only if the total host residency is itself the intended measured condition.

“No production router touched” does NOT mean “side server has no memory impact”.

Unified memory is host-wide.

## Stage B evidence must prove actual residency

For condition A capture evidence that only the monster is resident.

For condition B capture evidence that BOTH intended model workers are resident concurrently during the measured workload.

Record:

- process/model identities;
- model files/hashes;
- worker PIDs/ports;
- resident/peak memory;
- wired memory;
- system memory pressure;
- swap delta;
- load/eviction/reload events;
- task outcomes;
- latency p50/p95;
- monster throughput;
- utility invocation/hit rate;
- OOM/Metal/backend errors;
- complete raw logs.

A preset listing two models is NOT residency evidence.

## Stop conditions

Abort immediately on the first structural safety failure, including:

- Metal Compute / Insufficient Memory error;
- memory-pressure threshold breach;
- unexpected swap growth beyond predeclared bound;
- monster eviction when simultaneous residency is required;
- production router/session interference;
- unexpected third model load;
- host-budget violation;
- corrupted/uninterpretable telemetry.

Do not blind-retry after a Compute error.

One structural failure is data.

## Final experiment outcomes

Allow honest outcomes:

`PASS`
= simultaneous residency achieved and all predeclared benefit/safety thresholds met.

`FAIL_BENEFIT`
= pair residency works but does not earn its memory/performance cost.

`FAIL_RESIDENCY`
= both models cannot remain resident together.

`UNSAFE`
= memory/Metal/runtime stop condition triggered.

`INVALID`
= experiment was contaminated or telemetry insufficient.

Any of these can complete the experiment if the run was valid and evidence is complete.

Do not keep retrying until B wins.

## Current lifecycle truth

For now record:

`stage_A_offline_source = retain/review`
`stage_A_acceptance = pending independent verification`
`exclusive_window_approved = false`
`stage_B_live_smoke = not run`
`pair_residency_qualified = false`
`goal_terminal = false`

